e help text and the docs quote')","norm_id":"nf8816fa737a70fcb","priority":0.066,"reason":"low-validity","recalled":false,"scenarios":["Executor writes one figure in help text and a rounded/stale figure in AGENTS.md, reproducing a doc-vs-target divergence"],"severity":null,"suggested_fix":"Add to the cost ACs: 'the identical measured figure appears in make verify help, AGENTS.md, docs/local-dev-env.md and docs/coverage.md.'","tier":"LLM","validity":0.25,"verification":{"binary":{"absence_confirmed_in_context":"yes","asserted_capability_confirmed":"na","cited_reference_accurate":"yes","claims_absence":"yes","committed_work_relies_on_unbacked_claim":"na","current_state_satisfies_plan_goal":"na","evidence_entails_finding":"no","impact_follows_necessarily":"no","is_verifiable":"yes","no_existing_mitigation":"no","no_viable_alternative_explanation":"no","path_reachable":"yes","prerequisite_attribution_valid":"na","respects_artifact_altitude":"no","severity_claim_justified":"no"},"severity_attributes":{"ac_unverifiable":"none","blast_radius":"local","debt_impact":"low","divergent_implementation":"none","dod_uncertifiable":"none","internal_conflict":"none","irreversible_without_rationale":"none","likelihood":"medium","prod_impact":"none","reversibility":"easy","silent_vs_self_revealing":"self_revealing","undecomposed":"none","vague_directive":"low"}}},{"block_threshold":0.75,"blocking_enabled":true,"checklist_item":"- [ ] Reconcile the 'pytest-only / make lint exit 0' claim for the mechanism-delta gate with Makefile:253 (`check_mechanism_delta.py --check` runs in `make lint`): state precisely which violation class the pytest oracle catches that `--check` does not, and confirm RED demo #1's stale-baseline-entry case actually leaves `make lint` green.","cohort":["E4"],"criteria":["E4"],"decision":"dropped","decision_margin":-0.75,"drop_reason":null,"evidence":["Makefile:253: `python scripts/check_mechanism_delta.py --check` runs INSIDE the `lint` target","Plan symptom table: 'tests/unit/test_mechanism_delta.py | change 2601 pushed red; make lint exit 0'","Plan RED demo #1: 'add a stale entry to .github/mechanism-baseline.json -> make verify fails in test_mechanism_delta.py while make lint still exits 0'","test_mechanism_delta.py:26-27 loads the same script (SCRIPT_PATH) and baseline (.github/mechanism-baseline.json) that make lint's --check invocation uses","check_mechanism_delta.py comment (Makefile:242-252): 'REMOVING one is always allowed (it buckets as stale)' — so a stale/removed baseline entry does not fail --check"],"finding":"The plan asserts the mechanism-delta gate is 'pytest-only' and that `make lint` exits 0 on a mechanism violation (symptom table row for test_mechanism_delta.py; RED demo #1), but `make lint` invokes `python scripts/check_mechanism_delta.py --check` at Makefile:253 — the same ratchet the pytest oracle wraps. The claim only holds if the pytest test catches a violation class `--check` does not (e.g. a stale baseline entry, which the shrink-only ratchet ALLOWS as a removal, versus test_mechanism_delta.py asserting canonical/exact baseline shape). The plan never states this distinction, so as written the premise contradicts make lint's actual contents.","group_criteria":null,"group_id":null,"id":"f1c421ec5904841da","impact":0.0,"is_primary":null,"location":"Symptom table (row: tests/unit/test_mechanism_delta.py) and Testing § RED demonstration #1","norm_id":"n0c66fa1319070716","priority":0.0,"reason":"low-validity","recalled":false,"scenarios":["The commit author runs `make lint` after adding a stale mechanism-baseline entry; if `--check` also reddens, RED demo #1's 'make lint still exits 0' does not reproduce and the demo fails to show the divergence the ticket needs to prove.","A reviewer reading the symptom table concludes the mechanism gate is unreachable from make lint, when it is in fact partially reachable — undermining the whole 'lying proxy' framing for this one gate."],"severity":null,"suggested_fix":